{
  "family": "typography",
  "spec": "10-tokens/03-typography.md",
  "cssFile": "tokens/typography.css",
  "dartFile": "dart/monokit_typography.dart",
  "dartType": "MonokitTextStyle",
  "description": "IBM Plex, one superfamily, three registers: Sans for chrome and content, Serif strictly for reading surfaces, Mono for machine-shaped strings. Quiet chrome, loud content.",
  "axes": [
    "widthClass"
  ],
  "notes": [
    "D7: the IBM Plex superfamily. px is canonical; the rem values are the web pipeline's derived parity.",
    "The four display and headline roles are FLUID: they interpolate between the top of compact (600px) and the bottom of wide (1280px). Everything else is fixed at every width, because if a design wants bigger chrome on desktop the answer is density and spacing, not font size.",
    "Hierarchy spans one step: adjacent slots differ by at most one ramp step and/or one weight step.",
    "Weights 400/500/600/700 only, never below 400. 12px is the floor and nothing renders below it."
  ],
  "groups": {
    "families": {
      "sans": {
        "value": "\"IBM Plex Sans\",ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif"
      },
      "serif": {
        "value": "\"IBM Plex Serif\",ui-serif,Georgia,Cambria,serif",
        "description": "The reading register. The document reader and long-form body, nowhere else."
      },
      "mono": {
        "value": "\"IBM Plex Mono\",ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace",
        "description": "Machine-shaped strings the user reads rather than types."
      }
    },
    "weights": {
